# Docker build context.
#
# All three services build with `context: .`, so without this every image build
# ships the whole working tree to the daemon before copying three folders out
# of it. The local Chrome profiles under .autoqa alone were about a gigabyte,
# and data/audits.db another hundred megabytes — none of it reachable by any
# COPY in any Dockerfile.
#
# The Dockerfiles copy explicit paths rather than the whole tree, so this file
# is about build speed and context size, not about what ends up in the image.

.git
.gitignore

# QA harness state: Chrome profiles, run artifacts, screenshots. Regenerable.
.autoqa

# Server runtime state. Mounted as a volume in production, never baked in.
data

# Built extension output — the images serve the gateway and the public page.
dist

# Local tool installs and their caches.
.claude
.cursor
.impeccable
.github
node_modules
tools/cursor-webqa/node_modules

# Tests, fixtures and developer tooling: no service imports them.
tests
tools
fixtures
qa-sites
scripts

# Documentation and release paperwork.
docs
*.md
!README.md
RELEASE_PROVENANCE.txt
Caddyfile.snippet
docker-compose*.yml

# Environments and editor noise.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.cursorignore
.cursorindexingignore
*.log
